#Definition of Done (DoD)
        What:
        Definition of Done is a shared checklist/criteria that defines when a User Story or Increment is considered complete and ready.

        Purpose:

        Ensure consistent quality
        Define clear completion criteria
        Avoid incomplete work being considered finished
        Ensure the Increment meets the required quality standards

        Typical DoD:

        Development completed
        Code reviewed
        Unit/API/UI tests completed
        QA testing completed
        Critical defects fixed
        Regression completed
        Documentation updated if required
        Acceptance Criteria satisfied

        QA Role:
        QA verifies that the story meets the DoD before considering it complete.

        Interview Answer:

        "Definition of Done is a shared set of criteria agreed by the Scrum Team that must be satisfied for a User Story or Increment to be considered complete. It ensures that the work is properly developed, tested, and meets the required quality standards."

